# Template for demo mode (`npm run dev:demo`). Copy it to `.env.demo.local`:
#
#   cp .env.demo.local.example .env.demo.local
#
# and fill in the two secrets below to get a local demo that behaves exactly
# like the hosted one at https://challenger-phi.vercel.app/ — same AI Configs,
# same model calls, same judges and traces, still with no database.
#
# Copy to `.env.demo.local`, NOT to `.env.demo`: `.env.demo` is committed on
# purpose (it's what makes a fresh checkout and the CI demo job run with no
# setup at all), so a key written there is one `git add` away from being
# public. `.env.demo.local` is gitignored, and Vite loads it last, so it wins
# over both `.env` and `.env.demo`.
#
# Everything the hosted demo runs with is listed here. The first three come
# from vercel.json at build and runtime and are already set for you in
# .env.demo; the two secrets come from the Vercel project's environment
# variables, which is why they can't be committed here.

# --- Already in .env.demo — override only if you need to ---------------------

# Selects the in-memory dataset and the demo login flow instead of Postgres +
# better-auth. Without it the app boots into database mode and needs a real
# DATABASE_URL.
DEMO_MODE=true

# The dev server's own origin. 5173 is `npm run dev:demo`; use 4173 if you're
# pointing this at `npm run preview`.
ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173

# Demo mode never verifies a session against a database, so this is a
# placeholder rather than a secret — the same literal value vercel.json uses.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=demo-mode-not-a-real-secret

# LaunchDarkly client-side ID — exposed to the browser, not a secret. The app
# falls back to this exact production ID when it's unset, so browser flags,
# the experiment, and session replay already work on a bare checkout. Set it
# only to point a local demo at a different LD environment.
PUBLIC_LD_CLIENT_ID="6a761baeb7c4670ad5fc4aee"

# --- The two secrets, both [OPTIONAL] ----------------------------------------
#
# Neither is required to boot — the app degrades instead of failing. They're
# what the hosted demo has and a bare checkout doesn't, so fill them in when you
# want a local run that matches it.

# [OPTIONAL] LaunchDarkly server-side SDK key — SECRET, never PUBLIC_-prefixed.
# Distinct from the client-side ID above: that one only drives browser flag
# evaluation, while this is what lets the server resolve AI Configs and report
# generation metrics, judge results, and traces. Without it the server SDK never
# initializes, every tracker call no-ops, and an AI Config's Monitoring tab
# stays empty no matter how much the feature is used.
LAUNCHDARKLY_SDK_KEY=""

# [OPTIONAL] Anthropic (server-side only — used by the AI score-scan feature).
# The app runs fine without it, but the AI features do not work: photo scoring
# and text parsing return randomized placeholder scores instead of reading your
# card, and the score chat answers every message with "Logging a mock reading —
# no Anthropic API key is configured" rather than filling in the match form.
# Leave it empty to demo that fallback on purpose; fill it in and every scan and
# chat turn is a real, billed model call.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# --- Also optional, and not set on the hosted demo ----------------------------

# Upstash/Vercel KV. Only meaningful on a serverless deploy, where it persists
# demo-mode writes across instances; a local demo already keeps them in the
# server process. Unset on the hosted demo today, so leaving these empty is the
# closer match to production.
KV_REST_API_URL=""
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=""
